# Code and implementation

## Formatting

- Formatting: ESLint (tabs, single quotes, semicolons, chained-call newlines). Run `npm run format` or `eslint src/ --fix`.
- Stylelint: BEM (`.block__element--modifier`), SCSS vars/mixins kebab-case, no IDs, no `!important`, max specificity 0,4,0. Run `npm run lint:styles`.

## Imports and Vue

- Use `@/` alias for imports from `src`; avoid relative paths when `@/` applies.
- Vue: `<script setup>` only; external SCSS via `<style src="./ComponentName.scss" lang="scss" scoped />` (no closing tag). No large inline style blocks. Template: when a tag has more than one attribute, one attribute per line and closing `>` on its own line (see vue-template-attributes rule).
- View-specific modules live in `views/{ViewName}/`; shared modules in `shared/modules/`. View imports: relative for view modules; `@/` for shared. Tests colocated in `__tests__/` next to component.

## Store, routing, i18n

- Pinia: `defineStore`; split state, actions, getters. Async actions: `try/catch` (and `finally` if needed); manage `loading`/`error`. Store calls `core/services` for data.
- Routing: hash history (`createWebHashHistory`); routes map to components in `views`.
- i18n: `$t('key.path')` for UI strings; keys in `src/locale/{lang}.json`; no hardcoded UI strings where i18n is expected.

## Code style (ESLint)

- No magic numbers (named constants). No `else`. All `if` use `{}`. No ambiguous conditions; no truthy/falsy without explicit intent.
- No side effects in `map`/`filter`; `map` for return values only. `async/await` with `try/catch`. No `innerHTML` without sanitization. Multiline when multiple attributes on a tag.

## Naming

- English only. camelCase (vars, functions); UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (constants). Booleans: prefix with `is`, `has`, `can`, `should`, or `needs`. Descriptive; no abbreviations unless standard and documented.
- Layer-appropriate: domain = business language; services = use cases; API = resource/endpoint; store actions = state change. No names that hide IO or wrong layer.
